### 1. Variables

Variables are used to store values in Python.

`python
name = "Manasa"
age = 19
2. Data Types

Python provides different built-in data types.

Data Type	Example
int	10
float	10.5
str	"Python"
bool	True / False
NoneType	None

To check the type of a value:

x = 10
print(type(x))
3. Output — print()

The print() function is used to display output.

print("Hello, Python!")
print("Age:", 19)
4. User Input — input()

The input() function is used to receive input from the user.

name = input("Enter your name: ")
print(name)

input() returns a string by default.

5. Type Casting

Type casting means converting a value from one data type to another.

age = int(input("Enter your age: "))
height = float(input("Enter your height: "))

Common type-casting functions:

int()
float()
str()
bool()
6. F-Strings

F-strings are used to insert variables directly into strings.

name = "Manasa"
age = 19

print(f"My name is {name} and I am {age} years old.")
